### What is an Operating System?
> Interface between Hardware and Software 

1. In the linux we are running a Program so the linux is installed in the hardware 
2. First we need to know where am I currently 
  1. pwd - print working directory 
  2. ls - list of directories 
(**ll is a shortcut for ls -la**)
3. ls -l -a(when we use -a we get all the files including the hidden files)
4. . - is the current directory
5. .. - is the previous directory 
6. mkdir - create directory
    - for using already created path we need to use mkdir -p <path>
